@startuml 03-sequence-command
' Sequence diagram: generic command processing after game start.
' Concrete example: CommandMessage("PLACE bob B").

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceParticipant {
    BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
    BorderColor #888855
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF3CD
}

title MESOS — Generic Command Processing (after start)

actor "TCP Client\n(bob)" as C
actor "TCP Client\n(alice)" as CB
participant "TcpClientHandler" as TCH
participant "BlockingQueue\n<ClientMessage>" as BQ
participant ControllerWorker as CW
participant "CommandMessage\n.process()" as CM
participant Controller as CTRL
participant Game as G
participant "ModelListener\n→ CallBack" as ML
participant ServerRegistry as SR

note over C, SR
    Concrete message: CommandMessage("PLACE bob B")
    All post-start commands go through CommandMessage.
    No PlaceMessage, EndRoundMessage etc. — CommandMessage is the definitive solution.
end note

C -> TCH : writeObject(CommandMessage("PLACE bob B"))
TCH -> BQ : queue.put(msg)

note right of BQ
    TcpClientHandler is multi-threaded:
    each client has its own thread.
    The queue serializes access.
end note

BQ -> CW : take() — CommandMessage
CW -> CM : msg.setRegistry(registry)
CW -> CM : msg.process(controller)

CM -> CTRL : processCmd("PLACE bob B")
CTRL -> G : placeTotem(player_bob, offerTile_B)

G --> ML : PropertyChangeEvent("update", null, null)

ML -> SR : broadcast(SnapshotMessage.from(game))
SR -> C : sendMessage(SnapshotMessage)
SR -> CB : sendMessage(SnapshotMessage)

note right
    All connected clients
    receive the updated
    snapshot automatically.
end note

CTRL --> CM : "OK PLACE bob → B"
CM -> C : sendMessage(OkMessage("PLACE bob → B"))

== Case: unregistered nick (error) ==

note over TCH, BQ
    If the sender is not in the registry,
    TcpClientHandler throws RemoteException
    and does not enqueue the message.
end note

== Disconnection during the game ==

note over TCH, SR
    If IOException in the game loop:
    TcpClientHandler calls
    registry.handleDisconnection(nick)
    → views.remove(nick)
    → broadcast(ErrMessage("PLAYER_DISCONNECTED bob"))
end note

@enduml
